# Generated count files. Every PR that adds/removes a file, test, or line would
# change these if it committed them — the source of the O(n^2) "counter cascade".
#
# Under the reconcile model these files are NOT hand-committed in PRs: the
# DocOps gate treats their counts as advisory (--counts-advisory), and
# .github/workflows/docops-reconcile-main.yml regenerates them on push:main from
# the tree. So PRs leave these lines identical to main and they never conflict in
# the merge queue.
#
# `merge=union` is a defensive net only: if a PR ever does touch a count line, a
# union merge auto-resolves it (no hard conflict that would kick the PR from the
# queue) and the next push:main reconcile recomputes the authoritative value.
docs/docops/AUTO_INVENTORY.md merge=union
docs/governance/SOVEREIGN_MANIFEST.md merge=union

# State dashboard (morning brief). This file is independently refreshed by multiple
# agents/PRs in short windows. `merge=union` prevents a hard conflict block and
# lets a merge proceed — the result may need a quick cleanup pass to remove
# duplicate sections, but it never stops the PR from being mergeable.
# The `docops-reconcile-main.yml` pattern (regenerate after merge) is the right
# long-term model for this file if it grows further in churn.
docs/state/LIVE_OPS_DASHBOARD.md merge=union
